    <statement><p>Solve the equations below exactly.  Give your answers in radians,
and find all possible values for <m>t</m> in the interval
<m>0 \leq t \leq 2 \pi</m>.  If there is more than one answer,
enter your solutions in a comma separated list.</p>
<p>(a) <m>\displaystyle \sin{(t)} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}</m> when <m>t =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) <m>\displaystyle \cos{(t)} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}</m> when <m>t =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(c) <m>\displaystyle \tan{(t)} = -\sqrt{3}</m> when <m>t =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
