    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



(a) Since <m>\displaystyle \sin{(t)} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}</m>, we have <m>t= \pi/3 , (2 \pi)/3</m>.



(b) Since <m>\displaystyle \cos{(t)} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}</m>, we have <m>t= \pi/4 , (7 \pi)/4</m>.



(c) Since <m>\displaystyle \tan{(t)} = -\sqrt{3}</m>, we have <m>t= (2 \pi)/3 , (5 \pi)/3</m>.



</solution>
